WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Who's involved?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.731
The platform owner owns this gate,
moves each ring under a change record,

3
00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:08.400
and reviews the exclusions each quarter.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.649
The security operations
center reviews blocks and

5
00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:15.200
tampering attempts every week,
alongside the drift list.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.129
The operator collects a
sample of device states

7
00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:20.838
per ring per site and
works the drift tickets.

8
00:00:20.838 --> 00:00:24.649
One caution: the fixtures
are eleven fictional devices.

9
00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:27.402
On a real fleet, sample per ring per site,

10
00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:30.413
as the guide's post-change
validation says.

11
00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:33.840
The coverage check in Chapter
2 is the fleet-wide view.
